---
import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="Terms governing the use of the PayDart Android application, website, and open-source distribution."
  lastUpdated="September 2026"
>
  <div class="space-y-8 text-zinc-300">
    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-3">1. Acceptance of Terms</h2>
      <p class="mb-4">
        By downloading, installing, compiling, or using PayDart (the "Application") or accessing this website, you agree to be bound by these Terms of Service and the Apache 2.0 Open Source License. If you do not agree, do not install or use the Application.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-3">2. Nature of the Software</h2>
      <p class="mb-4">
        PayDart is an open-source, client-side Android utility designed to accelerate the scanning of Unified Payments Interface (UPI) QR codes and launch third-party UPI applications.
      </p>
      <p class="mb-4">
        <strong>Important Clarification:</strong> PayDart is NOT a bank, payment service provider (PSP), prepaid payment instrument (PPI), or digital wallet. PayDart does not hold funds, intermediate transactions, settle balances, or process payments.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-3">3. Disclaimer of Warranties</h2>
      <p class="mb-4">
        THE APPLICATION IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, TITLE, AND NON-INFRINGEMENT.
      </p>
      <p class="mb-4">
        The authors and contributors do not warrant that the application will be uninterrupted, error-free, or compatible with every specific merchant QR code standard or camera hardware.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-3">4. Limitation of Liability</h2>
      <p class="mb-4">
        IN NO EVENT SHALL THE AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES, LOSS OF DATA, FINANCIAL DISCREPANCIES, OR OTHER LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM, OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE SOFTWARE.
      </p>
      <p>
        Users are solely responsible for reviewing payment details (payee name, VPA, and amount) on the final payment confirmation screen of their selected UPI application before confirming any financial transaction with their UPI PIN.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-3">5. Trademark Disclaimers</h2>
      <p>
        "UPI" and "BHIM" are registered trademarks of the National Payments Corporation of India (NPCI). "Google Pay" is a trademark of Google LLC. "PhonePe" is a trademark of PhonePe Private Limited. "Paytm" is a trademark of One97 Communications Limited. "CRED" is a trademark of Dreamplug Technologies Pvt Ltd. PayDart is an independent project and is not endorsed by, sponsored by, or affiliated with NPCI or any third-party payment provider.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</LegalLayout>
